  "description": "The deployment is using API version **v1** and identifies itself with the user\u2011agent string **\u201cMyAppAgent/1.0.\u201d** The registrar is configured for the **External** interface, listening on **0.0.0.0** while advertising the external address **203.0.113.5**. Local networks **10.0.0.0/8** and **192.168.0.0/16** are recognized, record\u2011routing is enabled, and the system reports the address information entries \u201cinfo1\u201d and \u201cinfo2\u201d.  \n\nThe REST service runs in secured mode on port **8080**, bound to **0.0.0.0**, with a thread pool ranging from a minimum of **10** threads to a maximum of **200** threads and a timeout of **30,000\u202fms**. Its TLS assets are stored in **keystore.jks** and **truststore.jks**, both protected by the password **\u201cchangeit.\u201d** Data persistence is provided by a PostgreSQL source. Security is tightened with debugging turned on, a dedicated keystore (**secKeystore.jks**) and truststore (**secTruststore.jks**) secured by the password **\u201cs3cr3t,\u201d** using the **jks** store type. The client side negotiates the protocols **TLSv1.2** and **TLSv1.1** and requires authentication (**Enabled**). Access control permits traffic from **192.168.1.0/24** and denies the broader **10.0.0.0/8** range.  \n\nTransport listeners are defined for both **TCP** on port **5060** and **TLS** on port **5061**, each bound to **0.0.0.0**.",
  "reference_json": {
    "apiVersion": "v1",
    "metadata": {
      "userAgent": "MyAppAgent/1.0"
    },
    "spec": {
      "registrarIntf": "External",
      "bindAddr": "0.0.0.0",
      "externAddr": "203.0.113.5",
      "localnets": [
        "10.0.0.0/8",
        "192.168.0.0/16"
      ],
      "recordRoute": true,
      "addressInfo": [
        "info1",
        "info2"
      ],
      "restService": {
        "unsecured": false,
        "port": 8080,
        "maxThreads": 200,
        "minThreads": 10,
        "timeOutMillis": 30000,
        "bindAddr": "0.0.0.0",
        "keyStore": "keystore.jks",
        "trustStore": "truststore.jks",
        "keyStorePassword": "changeit",
        "trustStorePassword": "changeit"
      },
      "dataSource": {
        "provider": "postgresql"
      },
      "securityContext": {
        "debugging": true,
        "keyStore": "secKeystore.jks",
        "trustStore": "secTruststore.jks",
        "keyStorePassword": "s3cr3t",
        "keyStoreType": "jks",
        "client": {
          "protocols": [
            "TLSv1.2",
            "TLSv1.1"
          ],
          "authType": "Enabled"
        }
      },
      "accessControlList": {
        "allow": [
          "192.168.1.0/24"
        ],
        "deny": [
          "10.0.0.0/8"
        ]
      },
      "transport": [
        {
          "protocol": "tcp",
          "port": 5060,
          "bindAddr": "0.0.0.0"
        },
        {
          "protocol": "tls",
          "port": 5061,
          "bindAddr": "0.0.0.0"
        }
      ]
    }
